' Enterprise Agentic / Autonomous matrix visualization
'
' Per CR-ES-011 §20 + ADR-ES-010 §13 + ADR-ES-011 §5 + §11.
' Illustrates the four-state matrix that distinguishes the
' Agentic Enterprise and Autonomous Enterprise classifications.
'
' Authored by: Emmanuel A. Otchere (cardinal author rule, 2026-09-24)

@startuml enterprise-agentic-autonomous-matrix

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor #F0F8FF
    BorderColor #4682B4
    FontColor #000000
}

skinparam arrow {
    Color #2F4F4F
    FontColor #2F4F4F
}

title Enterprise, Agentic / Autonomous Matrix

rectangle "State 1: Neither\n(Conventional / Mixed)" as state1 #F5F5F5
rectangle "State 2: Agentic only\n(Agentic Enterprise)" as state2 #FFE4B5
rectangle "State 3: Autonomous only\n(Autonomous Enterprise)" as state3 #FFE4E1
rectangle "State 4: Both\n(Agentic + Autonomous Enterprise)" as state4 #E6E6FA

state1 --> state2 : add Agentic
state1 --> state3 : add Autonomous
state2 --> state4 : add Autonomous
state3 --> state4 : add Agentic

note bottom of state4
  Per ADR-ES-011 §11:
  State 4 is a valid combination of semantic
  characteristics. It does NOT result in
  creation of a new canonical concept. The
  two specialisations are independent semantic
  dimensions per AE-AUTO-CON-013.
end note

@enduml
